        "message": "LU-20869 tests: cut sanity-sec 31 tunefs and MMP waits\n\ntest_31 and cleanup_31 run about 40 serial tunefs calls per pass,\nthree or more per target, each with its own ssh and a stop and\nwriteconf round trip. The servicenode tunefs on mds1 also turns on\nldiskfs MMP, after which every tunefs and mount of mds1 waits 11s\nfor the MMP check, six tunefs calls in cleanup alone.\n\nDo two tunefs per target, one to erase the old mgsnode and one to\nset the new one with writeconf, with the mds1 service node options\nin the same calls, on all targets in parallel. The two must stay\nseparate: on ZFS a key erased and set in one call is stored with a\nleading ':'. The parallel calls use parallel_start() with a new\nTUNEFS operation, so PARALLEL_OPS=0 or PARALLEL_TUNEFS=0 serializes\nthem. When mds1 had no failover node before the test, pass\n--skipmmp so MMP is not enabled, on servers new enough to have it.\n\ncleanup_31 restored an existing mds1 failover node with\n--servicenode, though the framework formats with --failnode, so\nmds1 was left with only its partner as a service node and could\nnot mount. Restore it with the option it was set with.\n\nOn a 2 MDS (2 MDT each), 1 OSS (4 OST) ldiskfs VM cluster, test 31\ntook 415, 407 and 402s before and 312, 291 and 291s after. CI\nruns it 6972 times per 30 days at a mean of 548s; at about 100s\nsaved on ldiskfs and less on ZFS, that is roughly 150 hours.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=31\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=31\nFixes: f70821fc14 (\"LU-16775 tests: cleanup target after sanity-sec test_31\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iaf833bb42bf91925e76f33775405fe8d753eee89\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
